 ## Background
-SurfelNeRF was introduced in 2023 by researchers investigating the combination of classical 3D reconstruction and NeRF for online photorealistic reconstruction of large-scale indoor scenes [S1]. It builds on the concept of neural surfels, extending classical surfel-based fusion schemes to the neural setting. The method was evaluated on the ScanNet dataset, demonstrating state-of-the-art performance in both feedforward and per-scene optimization settings [S1].
+SurfelNeRF was introduced in 2023 by researchers investigating the combination of classical 3D reconstruction and NeRF for online photorealistic reconstruction of large-scale indoor scenes [S1]. It builds on the concept of neural surfels, extending classical surfel-based fusion schemes to the neural setting [S1]. The method was evaluated on the ScanNet dataset, demonstrating state-of-the-art performance in both feedforward and per-scene optimization settings [S1].
 
